# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/octo-3 window (octo-T8 and its three levers on the fused stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/octo-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq arm needs its binary; every other arm runs that
# binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# Z: the window's end: status and an all-four reset, no agent start (the cards stay under development). The owner restores the ARC runner sets to their normal scale, then
# production: card reset, link measurement, topology republish, agent restart, deploy and the post-checks. Duration (estimate): 10 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1
